\pxsm0.8;{\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;NOTES:\P\H0.8x;\P\fArial|b0|i0|c134|p34;1\fSimSun|b0|i0|c134|p2;.\P\P\fArial|b0|i0|c134|p34;2\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;. This single-line diagram (SLD) is provided for visual representation only and is not drawn to scale.\P\
  3
P\fArial|b0|i0|c134|p34;3\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;. Provide appropriate strain relief at all harness, LYNX, transition, and equipment connection points.\P\P\psm1;\fArial|b0|i0|c134|p34;4\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;. String polarity shall be verified before conn
  3
ecting the PV harness or LYNX assembly. Do not reverse positive and\fArial|b0|i0|c134|p34; \fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;negative connections.\P\psm0.9;\P\psm1;\fArial|b0|i0|c134|p34;5\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;. Installation shall comply with the applicable NEC re
  3
quirements,\fArial|b0|i0|c134|p34; \fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;local codes, approved listings, project specifications, and the authority having jurisdiction.\P\psm0.9;\P\psm1;\fArial|b0|i0|c134|p34;6\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;. All connectors shall be fully engag
  3
ed, locked, and protected from mechanical damage, moisture,\fArial|b0|i0|c134|p34; \fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;contamination, and direct\fArial|b0|i0|c134|p34; \fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;contact with the ground.\P\psm0.8;\P\fArial|b0|i0|c134|p34;7\fArial|b0|i0|c0
  1
|p34;. Field connections shall be installed using the manufacturer-specified tools and torque requirements.\P\P\fArial|b0|i0|c134|p34;8\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;. Maintain the minimum cable-bending radius specified by the cable and assembly manufacturer.}
